linuxmuster-opnsense (7.3.3) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Switch the changelog distribution from unstable to lmn73: the version
    scheme is 7.<line>.<n> and the distribution names the linuxmuster.net
    line the package is built for (faircomp package conventions).
  * Declare the linuxmuster line in Depends: linuxmuster-tools7 (>= 7.3),
    linuxmuster-tools7 (<< 7.4). opn-update-aliases imports
    linuxmusterTools.devices, and the hooks live in the hook directories of
    linuxmuster-tools7 (group-manager) and linuxmuster-base7 (device import).
  * Packaging: source format 3.0 (native), Rules-Requires-Root: no,
    Standards-Version 4.6.2, Homepage, English package description,
    debian/copyright and LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later), .gitignore for build
    artifacts.
  * Build with "make deb" (dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -tc) instead of
    buildpackage.sh; debian/rules keeps debhelper away from the wrapper
    Makefile.
  * CI: fast tier (py_compile, ruff, shellcheck), package build in the
    lmndev-runner container chosen by the changelog distribution, install
    smoke on Ubuntu 24.04; release workflow with the tag == changelog gate,
    prerelease for -rc tags, .deb and .changes attached to the release.
  * Unify the maintainer address to Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>.
  * Rename readme.md to README.md and document the installation.
  * No functional changes since 7.3.2.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

linuxmuster-opnsense (7.3.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Support syncing multiple schools onto one firewall:
    - New per-school "school_prefix" ([aliases]) prepended to every alias name
      so schools no longer collide on a shared firewall.
    - Alias names that would exceed OPNsense's 32-char limit are shortened
      deterministically with a short hash suffix instead of silently truncated.
    - Aliases are stamped with an owner-school marker; an alias owned by a
      different school is never overwritten (skipped with a warning and a
      non-zero exit) to prevent silent data loss.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <k.stenzel@fair-comp.de>  Tue, 07 Jul 2026 10:41:39 +0200

linuxmuster-opnsense (7.3.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Treat OPNsense HTTP 200 responses with result=failed as errors instead of
    silently reporting success.
  * Sanitize alias names to the OPNsense-allowed character set so roles/rooms
    with hyphens (e.g. classroom-studentcomputer) sync correctly.
  * opn-update-all-schools: continue with the remaining schools when one fails.
  * opn-update-aliases: skip devices without an IP and reconfigure only once
    instead of after every alias.
  * opn-captive-voucher: scope "delete --username" to the given group, make the
    deletion modes mutually exclusive, reject negative time values, and report
    the actual number of vouchers created.
  * opn-captive-sessions: make --kill-username and --kill-sessionid mutually
    exclusive.
  * Handle PUT requests and guard delete_alias against non-dict API responses.
  * Packaging: build with dh-python.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <k.stenzel@fair-comp.de>  Tue, 07 Jul 2026 09:10:48 +0200

linuxmuster-opnsense (7.3.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add HTTP request timeouts to avoid hanging hooks/CLI commands.
  * URL-encode alias and voucher path segments for safe API endpoints.
  * Validate school names before building configuration file paths.

